repository-code: 'https://github.com/kongfundamentals/SpecimIQ-Absolute-Radiance-Calibration'
abstract: >-
  Code and data to reproduce the figures and tables of the paper
  "Measuring Absolute Radiance by Calibrating a Hyperspectral Camera
  Economically". A commercial hyperspectral camera (Specim IQ) is
  characterised (repeatability, linearity, dark current, spatial
  uniformity, wavelength calibration) and calibrated for absolute
  spectral radiance with a factory-calibrated spectroradiometer.
  The calibration is validated with an OLED panel and a Macbeth
  ColorChecker. The package contains the raw hyperspectral images,
  the spectroradiometer and colour camera data, and MATLAB code.
keywords:
  - Hyperspectral imaging
  - Absolute spectral radiance
  - Camera calibration
  - Spectral radiance calibration
  - Specim IQ
  - Lighting appearance model
